# ─── cap-online .gitignore ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Principle: no binary files in git. Source/text (.md, .html, .py, .json,
# .csv, small .svg) is tracked; everything heavy or binary is excluded.

# Documents / office binaries
**/*.pdf
**/*.docx
**/*.doc
**/*.pptx
**/*.ppt
**/*.xlsx
**/*.xls

# Images (raster)
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.png
**/*.gif
**/*.bmp
**/*.tiff
**/*.tif
**/*.webp
**/*.psd
**/*.ico

# Audio
**/*.mp3
**/*.wav
**/*.m4a
**/*.aac
**/*.flac
**/*.ogg

# Video
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov
**/*.mkv
**/*.avi
**/*.webm
**/*.wmv

# Fonts (binary) -- regenerate locally via tools/fetch_local_fonts.py, never commit the files.
# gfonts-local.css is generated alongside the font files by that same script (kept in
# sync with whatever font-file names it downloads), so it's excluded here too rather
# than committed and risking drifting out of sync with a freshly regenerated fonts/ folder.
**/*.woff2
**/*.woff
**/*.ttf
**/*.otf
**/*.eot
books/strategy-book/design/templates/vendor/gfonts-local.css

# Archives & executables / large binaries
**/*.zip
**/*.rar
**/*.7z
**/*.tar
**/*.gz
**/*.exe
**/*.dll
**/*.msi
**/*.bin
**/*.iso

# Base64-encoded image blobs (derived from images, kept local)
content/assets/green-screen/book-cover-image-base-64.txt

# Explicit heavy-source folders (kept local only)
materials/icai-source/
photo-gallery/originals/
obs-setup/recordings/
obs-setup/tools/

# ICAI downloaded PDFs + their converted MDs (regeneratable on demand)
tools/downloaded_pdfs/

# Telegram tool generated scan reports (local scratch output)
telegram/tools/_reports/

# Telegram bot runtime data (logs, user uploads — local only)
telegram/assets/myfiles_bot/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.python-version
pip-log.txt

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# Packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.spyproject
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
local_settings.py

# Databases (binary; e.g. Telegram bot analytics/logging DBs)
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# manage_bots.py runtime state (PID files, per-bot logs) -- local only
telegram/database/run/

# Test Mode: students' uploaded answer-sheet photos/documents -- binary +
# personal data, never committed (see TEST-MODE-ROADMAP.md §7's privacy note)
telegram/assets/exam_bot/Tests/uploads/

# Secrets / credentials -- never commit live tokens/keys
telegram/creds.txt
**/creds.txt
*.env
.env
books/bridge-course/YogaMembersListNameMumbers.md
books/concept-book/characters/animations/.thumbnail

# Node.js dependencies (tools/as19 and any future JS tooling)
node_modules/

# Comparator: full local mirror of a competitor's website (HTML/CSS/JS/images) --
# large, binary-heavy, and not our own content; local reference only
telegram/comparator/sales-agent/coceducation/site-mirror/
